1
00:00:25,826 --> 00:00:28,026
♪ ♪

2
00:00:36,370 --> 00:00:39,805
♪ ♪

3
00:00:49,350 --> 00:00:52,250
♪ ♪

4
00:01:20,413 --> 00:01:22,347
♪ ♪

5
00:01:51,545 --> 00:01:53,478
♪ ♪

6
00:02:21,809 --> 00:02:23,742
♪ ♪

7
00:02:31,318 --> 00:02:33,084
Ah.

8
00:02:40,494 --> 00:02:41,527
Fill me in.

9
00:02:41,595 --> 00:02:43,072
Your meeting's in
the conference room,

10
00:02:43,096 --> 00:02:45,008
and<i> Atlanta Tonight</i> wants
you at the station at 5:00.

11
00:02:45,032 --> 00:02:46,142
Fine. Here's the proof sheet

12
00:02:46,166 --> 00:02:47,511
from that photo
session yesterday.

13
00:02:47,535 --> 00:02:50,235
Oh. Oh. This one.
I look adorable.

14
00:02:50,303 --> 00:02:51,737
Have the prints
made up and sent out

15
00:02:51,805 --> 00:02:53,116
with the press release
on the takeover.

16
00:02:53,140 --> 00:02:54,339
Yes, ma'am.

17
00:02:56,410 --> 00:02:59,344
Maggie, Donald.

18
00:02:59,413 --> 00:03:02,079
Bobby.

19
00:03:02,149 --> 00:03:04,029
Chrissie. As always, a pleasure.

20
00:03:06,153 --> 00:03:08,253
Let's cut to the
chase, shall we?

21
00:03:08,321 --> 00:03:11,556
As you already know, the SEC
has approved my takeover plans.

22
00:03:11,625 --> 00:03:13,669
Within a week, I will control
each of your companies.

23
00:03:13,693 --> 00:03:16,695
Bobby, this is not personal.

24
00:03:16,764 --> 00:03:19,397
Not personal? My
company's my whole life.

25
00:03:19,466 --> 00:03:21,343
I created it with my
own blood, sweat

26
00:03:21,367 --> 00:03:22,579
and tears.

27
00:03:22,603 --> 00:03:23,869
Sugar.

28
00:03:23,938 --> 00:03:24,669
You're low, Katie.

29
00:03:24,738 --> 00:03:27,272
Heartless, low.

30
00:03:27,341 --> 00:03:28,785
But consistent.

31
00:03:28,809 --> 00:03:30,387
You still want the
same thing you wanted

32
00:03:30,411 --> 00:03:31,643
in the first grade.

33
00:03:31,712 --> 00:03:33,478
What did I want, Chrissie?

34
00:03:33,547 --> 00:03:35,247
More.

35
00:03:36,750 --> 00:03:39,017
Katie, you're a powerful
businesswoman.

36
00:03:39,086 --> 00:03:41,430
Given. But you're a lousy cook.

37
00:03:41,454 --> 00:03:42,820
Really, sugar?

38
00:03:42,889 --> 00:03:45,290
I'm the cookie lady.

39
00:03:45,359 --> 00:03:47,370
Maggie, you understand
why I'm doing this,

40
00:03:47,394 --> 00:03:48,993
don't you?

41
00:03:49,062 --> 00:03:50,228
Perfectly.

42
00:03:50,296 --> 00:03:53,765
I am taking over each
of your companies.

43
00:03:53,834 --> 00:03:57,202
Accept it gracefully and
you can keep your titles

44
00:03:57,271 --> 00:03:59,103
and salaries.

45
00:03:59,172 --> 00:04:00,383
Fight me,

46
00:04:00,407 --> 00:04:02,173
you'll wind up with zilch.

47
00:04:02,242 --> 00:04:04,743
Miss White, the bakery.

48
00:04:04,811 --> 00:04:05,922
It's an emergency.

49
00:04:05,946 --> 00:04:08,146
Think it over.

50
00:04:08,215 --> 00:04:10,882
Where are the samples
of my new line of cookies

51
00:04:10,951 --> 00:04:11,991
for the show tonight?

52
00:04:12,018 --> 00:04:13,385
They're in a tin on your desk.

53
00:04:13,453 --> 00:04:15,954
Good.

54
00:04:16,023 --> 00:04:18,089
You have 24 hours.

55
00:04:25,131 --> 00:04:26,664
Witch.

56
00:04:30,036 --> 00:04:31,316
Out of my way!

57
00:04:31,371 --> 00:04:33,149
Get back, please.
Let me through.

58
00:04:37,411 --> 00:04:38,877
Who did this?

59
00:04:38,945 --> 00:04:41,185
Miss White, there's
something wrong with this oven.

60
00:04:41,214 --> 00:04:42,258
It will be working fine,

61
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:43,660
then all of the
sudden, it goes berserk.

62
00:04:43,684 --> 00:04:45,450
I told you to fix it.

63
00:04:45,519 --> 00:04:48,053
I've had the repairman
out here five times.

64
00:04:48,121 --> 00:04:49,388
He never finds anything wrong.

65
00:04:49,456 --> 00:04:52,958
Well, you get him back out
here, show him this mess,

66
00:04:53,026 --> 00:04:55,238
and tell him that unless
he wants his fanny sued,

67
00:04:55,262 --> 00:04:57,329
he damn well better
find something wrong.

68
00:05:07,708 --> 00:05:09,441
And on the business front,

69
00:05:09,509 --> 00:05:12,244
rumors are rife
of a takeover bid

70
00:05:12,312 --> 00:05:15,447
in the cutthroat world
of designer cookies.

71
00:05:15,516 --> 00:05:18,082
Katie White, the founder
of Miss Katie's Cookies,

72
00:05:18,151 --> 00:05:20,151
is rumored to be
planning a takeover

73
00:05:20,220 --> 00:05:21,753
of several of her competitors.

74
00:05:21,822 --> 00:05:23,021
I talked to her earlier,

75
00:05:23,089 --> 00:05:25,156
and I asked Miss
White if it was true

76
00:05:25,225 --> 00:05:27,258
she was planning
a hostile takeover.

77
00:05:27,327 --> 00:05:29,060
Hostile?

78
00:05:29,128 --> 00:05:30,395
Little ol' me?

79
00:05:30,464 --> 00:05:35,200
Sugar, all I do is bake
the world's best cookies.

80
00:05:35,269 --> 00:05:36,701
We also talked to the heads

81
00:05:36,770 --> 00:05:38,715
of the companies
targeted for takeover:

82
00:05:38,739 --> 00:05:41,673
Donald Ware, the
founder of Health Cookies.

83
00:05:41,742 --> 00:05:45,343
Uh, no, no comment. No comment.

84
00:05:45,412 --> 00:05:47,712
Maggie Shore of
Margaret's Muffins.

85
00:05:47,781 --> 00:05:49,714
Was Miss White's
hostile takeover bid

86
00:05:49,783 --> 00:05:51,183
a surprise to you, Miss Shore?

87
00:05:51,251 --> 00:05:54,585
I don't know
anything about this.

88
00:05:54,655 --> 00:05:57,956
And Miss Chrissie Dubin, the
founder of the Pie Lady shops.

89
00:05:58,025 --> 00:06:00,392
No comment at this time.

90
00:06:01,528 --> 00:06:04,662
We also tried to
talk to Bobby Neil,

91
00:06:04,731 --> 00:06:07,298
of Bobby's Outrageous
Chocolate Chip Cookies.

92
00:06:07,368 --> 00:06:08,978
Mr. Neil, could we have
a comment about...?

93
00:06:09,002 --> 00:06:10,513
Get out of here! Get out!

94
00:06:10,537 --> 00:06:11,770
Mr. Neil, please! Mr. Neil?

95
00:06:15,275 --> 00:06:18,209
But rumor has it that
by tomorrow evening,

96
00:06:18,278 --> 00:06:19,543
we should know which way

97
00:06:19,612 --> 00:06:22,414
Atlanta's cookies
are going to crumble.

98
00:06:22,483 --> 00:06:24,248
Let's turn now to weather.

99
00:06:24,317 --> 00:06:28,186
You know, Bobby's
an old friend of mine.

100
00:06:28,254 --> 00:06:31,422
I was his first investor.

101
00:06:31,492 --> 00:06:32,702
Did pretty well.

102
00:06:32,726 --> 00:06:36,461
Hmm. Well, he sure
looks unhappy tonight.

103
00:06:36,530 --> 00:06:38,407
Oh, you should have
heard him on the phone

104
00:06:38,431 --> 00:06:40,543
when I told him there
wasn't much I could do

105
00:06:40,567 --> 00:06:41,499
about that takeover.

106
00:06:41,568 --> 00:06:42,500
It's a shame.

107
00:06:42,569 --> 00:06:43,613
He's worked really hard.

108
00:06:43,637 --> 00:06:47,005
I'm sure he's a wonderful guy,

109
00:06:47,073 --> 00:06:51,209
but Miss Katie's Cookies
are better than his.

110
00:06:52,612 --> 00:06:55,180
How can you say that?

111
00:06:55,248 --> 00:06:57,115
Her cookies are nothing

112
00:06:57,184 --> 00:07:00,585
but little, round,
brown blobs of grease.

113
00:07:00,654 --> 00:07:03,622
Miss Katie's cookies
are soft and chewy.

114
00:07:03,690 --> 00:07:07,091
Bobby's, you need a jackhammer.

115
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:10,495
Bobby's cookies are
crisp and crunchy.

116
00:07:10,564 --> 00:07:13,798
You want cereal to
be crisp and crunchy!

117
00:07:13,867 --> 00:07:16,367
You want cookies
to be soft and chewy!

118
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:23,108
You know, I always thought
of you as a man of great taste.

119
00:07:23,177 --> 00:07:26,044
Well, yeah.

120
00:07:26,113 --> 00:07:27,846
But your taste in cookies...

121
00:07:27,915 --> 00:07:29,480
is impeccable!

122
00:07:29,550 --> 00:07:31,394
Miss Katie's cookies are nothing

123
00:07:31,418 --> 00:07:33,685
but little, round,
brown blobs of grease.

124
00:07:33,754 --> 00:07:36,054
I'm going home.

125
00:07:36,122 --> 00:07:37,700
Well, what about dinner?

126
00:07:37,724 --> 00:07:39,057
Well, what are you fixing?

127
00:07:39,126 --> 00:07:40,659
Hot dogs.

128
00:07:40,727 --> 00:07:42,393
Pork or beef?

129
00:07:42,462 --> 00:07:44,663
Let's go out.

130
00:07:44,731 --> 00:07:47,298
You order yours,
I'll order mine.

131
00:07:47,367 --> 00:07:49,927
We'll talk about baseball.

132
00:07:55,875 --> 00:07:59,715
Can we focus up here
on beam number two?

133
00:07:59,746 --> 00:08:03,586
Yeah. Remember
we gotta check it here.

134
00:08:03,950 --> 00:08:05,910
I'll go check on Miss White.

135
00:08:08,589 --> 00:08:10,822
Just a little blush.

136
00:08:10,891 --> 00:08:12,991
My skin is perfect.

137
00:08:13,060 --> 00:08:14,859
Oh, and hollow
my cheeks a little.

138
00:08:14,928 --> 00:08:16,227
Don't want the viewers to think

139
00:08:16,296 --> 00:08:19,931
my cookies are fattening.

140
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:22,300
Bobby, what are you doing here?

141
00:08:22,368 --> 00:08:25,103
You gave us 24 hours to answer.

142
00:08:25,171 --> 00:08:26,171
Call my attorney.

143
00:08:26,206 --> 00:08:27,438
He's handling the takeover.

144
00:08:27,507 --> 00:08:28,673
What's the matter, Katie?

145
00:08:28,742 --> 00:08:31,910
Does the personal
approach make you nervous?

146
00:08:31,979 --> 00:08:33,712
You stay away from me.

147
00:08:33,780 --> 00:08:35,592
Somebody's got to
teach you a lesson, lady.

148
00:08:35,616 --> 00:08:38,382
Get a security guard.

149
00:08:38,451 --> 00:08:39,929
What's the matter
with you, Katie?

150
00:08:39,953 --> 00:08:42,320
You think it's okay
to take a man's life?

151
00:08:42,389 --> 00:08:46,024
I got nothing else:
no wife, no kids,

152
00:08:46,093 --> 00:08:48,293
just my business
to show for my life!

153
00:08:48,361 --> 00:08:49,294
Do you understand what

154
00:08:49,363 --> 00:08:50,363
I'm saying to you?

155
00:08:55,668 --> 00:08:56,601
Oh, thank God!

156
00:08:56,669 --> 00:08:57,869
Bobby Neil just threatened me.

157
00:08:57,937 --> 00:09:00,271
I want him removed immediately.

158
00:09:02,342 --> 00:09:04,475
Oh, he's gone.

159
00:09:08,648 --> 00:09:09,758
I've heard people say

160
00:09:09,782 --> 00:09:11,026
that they're addicted
to your cookies.

161
00:09:11,050 --> 00:09:12,562
Now, what do you put in them

162
00:09:12,586 --> 00:09:13,662
that makes them so good?

163
00:09:13,686 --> 00:09:14,931
Oh, I'm afraid that's a secret.

164
00:09:14,955 --> 00:09:16,265
Protecting your cookies, huh?

165
00:09:16,289 --> 00:09:17,289
Well, after all,

166
00:09:17,357 --> 00:09:19,357
there is a lot of
competition out there.

167
00:09:19,426 --> 00:09:20,669
Well, hey, there's nothing wrong

168
00:09:20,693 --> 00:09:21,853
with protecting your cookies.

169
00:09:22,829 --> 00:09:24,941
So what have you got in there?

170
00:09:24,965 --> 00:09:27,698
Well, it just so happens
I brought some samples

171
00:09:27,767 --> 00:09:29,400
of a brand-new
cookie I've developed.

172
00:09:29,469 --> 00:09:31,269
Goes on sale next week.

173
00:09:31,338 --> 00:09:33,604
I call it "The
Kitchen Sink Cookie"

174
00:09:33,673 --> 00:09:35,273
because it has everything in it:

175
00:09:35,342 --> 00:09:37,942
chocolate chips,
raisins, oatmeal.

176
00:09:38,011 --> 00:09:39,410
Yet it's soft like
all my cookies.

177
00:09:39,479 --> 00:09:42,146
Mm, that's outstanding.

178
00:09:42,215 --> 00:09:43,225
Aren't you gonna join me?

179
00:09:43,249 --> 00:09:44,516
Oh, be happy to.

180
00:09:44,584 --> 00:09:45,584
Hey, just one.

181
00:09:47,253 --> 00:09:48,987
So tell me,

182
00:09:49,055 --> 00:09:51,100
tell me the truth, do
you ever have a craving

183
00:09:51,124 --> 00:09:53,002
for just, say, a plain cracker?

184
00:09:58,332 --> 00:09:59,709
Better call the paramedic!

185
00:09:59,733 --> 00:10:01,532
Go to a commercial!

186
00:10:06,205 --> 00:10:08,806
Ben, the cops think
I killed Katie White.

187
00:10:08,875 --> 00:10:10,041
Well, I didn't.

188
00:10:10,110 --> 00:10:11,508
And they say I threatened her.

189
00:10:11,577 --> 00:10:12,643
Well, I didn't!

190
00:10:12,712 --> 00:10:14,779
I was just trying to talk
some sense into her!

191
00:10:14,848 --> 00:10:16,280
And, Ben, listen,

192
00:10:16,350 --> 00:10:19,517
that cookie tin, they
say I was alone with it.

193
00:10:19,586 --> 00:10:21,552
All right, maybe
I was, but I didn't

194
00:10:21,622 --> 00:10:23,054
put poison in it.

195
00:10:23,123 --> 00:10:25,323
Can I have a glass of water?

196
00:10:25,392 --> 00:10:29,394
Guard! Guard! Water!

197
00:10:29,462 --> 00:10:31,863
I did not doctor
those cookies, Ben.

198
00:10:31,931 --> 00:10:33,831
Hell, if I wanted to kill her,

199
00:10:33,900 --> 00:10:36,601
I'd just strangle her
with my own bare hands.

200
00:10:36,670 --> 00:10:37,969
Ben, listen!

201
00:10:38,038 --> 00:10:39,382
I am.

202
00:10:39,406 --> 00:10:41,183
Now, look, I know
what you're thinking.

203
00:10:41,207 --> 00:10:43,173
I didn't want her to buy me out.

204
00:10:43,242 --> 00:10:45,843
All right, I didn't,
but I did not kill her!

205
00:10:45,912 --> 00:10:46,912
You believe me?!

206
00:10:46,980 --> 00:10:48,947
Yeah.

207
00:10:49,016 --> 00:10:51,016
Well, why don't
you say something!

208
00:10:51,084 --> 00:10:55,587
It's hard to talk at 2:00
in the morning, Bobby.

209
00:10:59,659 --> 00:11:01,659
Well, hello, Ben.

210
00:11:03,263 --> 00:11:05,529
Who's the water for?

211
00:11:08,401 --> 00:11:10,601
Well, uh,

212
00:11:10,670 --> 00:11:14,139
Bob, you might as
well turn Bobby loose.

213
00:11:14,207 --> 00:11:15,852
He's not under
arrest or anything.

214
00:11:15,876 --> 00:11:18,709
You don't have anything to
hold him on. Come on, Bobby.

215
00:11:18,779 --> 00:11:22,446
Well, I'm very sorry, Ben,
but now he<i> is</i> under arrest.

216
00:11:22,515 --> 00:11:23,726
Oh, come on!

217
00:11:23,750 --> 00:11:25,583
Cookies indentical to the one

218
00:11:25,652 --> 00:11:28,619
that killed Katie White were
found in his garbage can.

219
00:11:28,689 --> 00:11:30,321
What?

220
00:11:43,870 --> 00:11:48,406
Maggie Shore, Donald Ware,
Bobby Neil and Chrissie Dubin,

221
00:11:48,475 --> 00:11:50,274
they were all here
when I came in

222
00:11:50,343 --> 00:11:52,343
to tell Katie she was
needed in the kitchen.

223
00:11:52,412 --> 00:11:54,556
Did, did everybody hear
you tell her about the cookie?

224
00:11:54,580 --> 00:11:57,115
I said I had put the
samples in her office.

225
00:11:57,183 --> 00:12:00,618
Well, maybe somebody got
in that cookie tin in her office

226
00:12:00,687 --> 00:12:03,021
before the TV station.

227
00:12:03,090 --> 00:12:04,655
It's right down the hall.

228
00:12:16,202 --> 00:12:17,735
Ah.

229
00:12:17,804 --> 00:12:19,336
Just got the police report.

230
00:12:19,406 --> 00:12:21,751
Katie White died of
anaphylactic shock.

231
00:12:21,775 --> 00:12:22,941
What's that?

232
00:12:23,009 --> 00:12:25,043
She was allergic to hazelnuts.

233
00:12:25,111 --> 00:12:26,855
That's what killed her? Yeah.

234
00:12:26,879 --> 00:12:28,524
That's why no one else
on the show was affected.

235
00:12:28,548 --> 00:12:30,014
Well, come on.

236
00:12:30,083 --> 00:12:31,928
Whoever heard of a
hazelnut killing anybody?

237
00:12:31,952 --> 00:12:34,685
There are some
people... Not a lot,

238
00:12:34,754 --> 00:12:37,721
but some... who are so allergic
to certain foods and medicines

239
00:12:37,790 --> 00:12:39,702
that the minute they take
them, they go into shock.

240
00:12:39,726 --> 00:12:42,205
Their blood pressure drops,
their heart can stop beating

241
00:12:42,229 --> 00:12:44,129
and they can die.

242
00:12:44,197 --> 00:12:45,329
Well, I'll be.

243
00:12:45,398 --> 00:12:47,531
Hazelnut.

244
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:49,645
You know, sometimes,
when I eat a bunch of them,

245
00:12:49,669 --> 00:12:50,713
I feel a little funny.

246
00:12:50,737 --> 00:12:51,937
I always thought it was gas.

247
00:12:51,972 --> 00:12:53,104
Allergic. She know it?

248
00:12:53,173 --> 00:12:54,772
Yeah.

249
00:12:54,840 --> 00:12:55,939
A lot of people did.

250
00:12:56,008 --> 00:12:57,853
Couple of years ago,
she was at a banquet

251
00:12:57,877 --> 00:12:59,087
for people in the food industry.

252
00:12:59,111 --> 00:13:00,523
Nobody told her
there were hazelnuts

253
00:13:00,547 --> 00:13:01,812
in the sauce for the chicken.

254
00:13:01,881 --> 00:13:04,148
She went into
shock, almost died.

255
00:13:04,216 --> 00:13:06,317
Well, put my leg
in a tea kettle.

256
00:13:06,386 --> 00:13:08,152
Hazelnuts. In here.

257
00:13:08,221 --> 00:13:09,320
Oh.

258
00:13:11,958 --> 00:13:13,969
I put a dozen cookies in the tin

259
00:13:13,993 --> 00:13:15,793
and left it sitting on
her desk, right there.

260
00:13:15,862 --> 00:13:17,294
That door always locked?

261
00:13:17,363 --> 00:13:18,607
Of course.

262
00:13:18,631 --> 00:13:21,191
No one would dare enter
without her permission.

263
00:13:22,435 --> 00:13:24,635
All of her cookies kind of
looked the same, didn't they?

264
00:13:24,704 --> 00:13:26,370
Yes.

265
00:13:26,439 --> 00:13:28,350
Whoever killed her
had to make sure

266
00:13:28,374 --> 00:13:30,352
that his cookies
looked just like hers.

267
00:13:30,376 --> 00:13:33,144
Do you know where
she kept the recipe?

268
00:13:33,213 --> 00:13:34,946
In a safe in the bakery.

269
00:13:45,124 --> 00:13:47,691
Coming through here.

270
00:13:50,129 --> 00:13:51,409
Not again!

271
00:14:07,881 --> 00:14:09,380
What the hell happened?

272
00:14:09,448 --> 00:14:10,614
I don't know.

273
00:14:10,683 --> 00:14:13,851
I put in the batter,
I set the timer,

274
00:14:13,919 --> 00:14:16,020
I turn it on and the
next thing I know,

275
00:14:16,089 --> 00:14:17,766
that thing's going a
zillion miles an hour.

276
00:14:17,790 --> 00:14:19,490
This is a brand-new machine!

277
00:14:19,559 --> 00:14:21,559
You must've done something.

278
00:14:21,628 --> 00:14:23,205
Hey, I'm telling you
what happened, okay?

279
00:14:23,229 --> 00:14:24,995
You, get this cleaned up here.

280
00:14:25,064 --> 00:14:26,208
Right away.

281
00:14:26,232 --> 00:14:27,977
This is the third
time in two weeks!

282
00:14:28,001 --> 00:14:30,001
Hey, I didn't do nothin'.

283
00:14:31,504 --> 00:14:33,605
<i>This is nice!</i>

284
00:14:33,673 --> 00:14:36,040
<i>Have you always
worked out of your home?</i>

285
00:14:36,109 --> 00:14:38,186
Fits in with the pie lady image.

286
00:14:38,210 --> 00:14:39,510
Thank you, Leticia.

287
00:14:39,578 --> 00:14:41,123
Here you go, a cup of coffee

288
00:14:41,147 --> 00:14:44,782
and a nice, warm
piece of rhubarb pie.

289
00:14:44,851 --> 00:14:45,984
Rhubarb!

290
00:14:46,052 --> 00:14:47,985
My favorite.

291
00:14:48,054 --> 00:14:49,798
I thought so.

292
00:14:49,822 --> 00:14:52,000
It's getting so I just
have to look at a person

293
00:14:52,024 --> 00:14:53,369
to know what
their favorite pie is.

294
00:14:53,393 --> 00:14:54,492
Mmm!

295
00:14:54,561 --> 00:15:00,164
My mother used to
make rhubarb pie.

296
00:15:00,233 --> 00:15:01,466
But I don't know...

297
00:15:01,534 --> 00:15:02,600
Mine's better?

298
00:15:02,668 --> 00:15:05,069
Daggone.

299
00:15:05,137 --> 00:15:07,504
Mmm, I believe it is.

300
00:15:09,242 --> 00:15:11,576
Well, I better get
down to business.

301
00:15:11,645 --> 00:15:12,743
So, Katie White.

302
00:15:12,811 --> 00:15:16,280
We were best friends,

303
00:15:16,349 --> 00:15:18,682
uh, lived right around
the corner from each other,

304
00:15:18,751 --> 00:15:22,253
went to grade school, high
school and college together,

305
00:15:22,322 --> 00:15:24,066
even went into
business together...

306
00:15:24,090 --> 00:15:25,233
Catering.

307
00:15:25,257 --> 00:15:26,857
Finish your pie.

308
00:15:26,926 --> 00:15:29,360
Well...

309
00:15:29,429 --> 00:15:31,162
Oh, you look very trim.

310
00:15:32,431 --> 00:15:35,800
Well, I, I try.

311
00:15:35,869 --> 00:15:39,303
But this is so good! Mm.

312
00:15:39,371 --> 00:15:42,439
What happened?

313
00:15:42,508 --> 00:15:43,707
Between you and Katie.

314
00:15:43,776 --> 00:15:46,177
Hmm, the man
she was in love with

315
00:15:46,245 --> 00:15:48,179
fell in love with me.

316
00:15:48,247 --> 00:15:51,983
While I was busy being in
love, she stole the business.

317
00:15:52,052 --> 00:15:53,984
Oh.

318
00:15:54,053 --> 00:15:57,188
And now she was gonna
steal your pie business.

319
00:15:57,257 --> 00:15:58,756
Oh.

320
00:15:58,824 --> 00:16:01,859
I can't get over this.

321
00:16:01,927 --> 00:16:04,295
I'm glad.

322
00:16:06,399 --> 00:16:07,598
After the meeting...

323
00:16:07,667 --> 00:16:09,133
With Katie.

324
00:16:09,202 --> 00:16:12,170
What did you do?

325
00:16:12,238 --> 00:16:14,004
We all left, I went home.

326
00:16:14,073 --> 00:16:15,772
Was your housekeeper...

327
00:16:15,841 --> 00:16:18,401
Oh, no, that was
her afternoon off.

328
00:16:18,978 --> 00:16:20,677
You're thinking

329
00:16:20,746 --> 00:16:23,947
I could've gone back,
slipped into Katie's office

330
00:16:24,016 --> 00:16:27,652
and put those hazelnut
cookies in that cookie tin.

331
00:16:27,720 --> 00:16:29,720
Could have,

332
00:16:29,788 --> 00:16:31,255
but didn't, Mr. Matlock.

333
00:16:31,324 --> 00:16:33,924
Well...

334
00:16:33,993 --> 00:16:37,061
you knew she was
allergic to hazelnuts.

335
00:16:37,130 --> 00:16:38,130
Everybody knew.

336
00:16:38,197 --> 00:16:39,596
She collapsed at a banquet

337
00:16:39,666 --> 00:16:41,143
in front of several
hundred people.

338
00:16:41,167 --> 00:16:43,100
Yeah.

339
00:16:45,605 --> 00:16:48,539
Oh, boy, this is good pie.

340
00:16:48,607 --> 00:16:51,342
I'm glad you enjoyed it.

341
00:16:51,411 --> 00:16:54,077
Well, like I say,
you give great pie.

342
00:16:54,146 --> 00:16:57,281
Oh, oh...

343
00:16:57,349 --> 00:17:00,184
You sure know how
to talk, don't you?

344
00:17:08,795 --> 00:17:09,871
Hi, Michelle. Hi.

345
00:17:09,895 --> 00:17:10,895
The usual?

346
00:17:10,930 --> 00:17:12,997
You bet. Blueberry muffin,

347
00:17:13,066 --> 00:17:14,231
cup of coffee to go.

348
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:15,878
That's wonderful,
right from the oven.

349
00:17:15,902 --> 00:17:18,469
You think you can take a break?

350
00:17:18,537 --> 00:17:20,104
Yeah.

351
00:17:20,173 --> 00:17:22,639
Um, bring it to the table. Sure.

352
00:17:22,708 --> 00:17:25,275
Jeannie, I'm taking
five. Okay, Maggie.

353
00:17:32,185 --> 00:17:33,362
Here you go. Thanks.

354
00:17:33,386 --> 00:17:35,286
Uh-huh, no problem. Thank you.

355
00:17:35,355 --> 00:17:38,255
Oh, boy.

356
00:17:38,324 --> 00:17:41,225
I've, uh, been expecting you.

357
00:17:41,294 --> 00:17:43,394
I heard that Ben is taking on

358
00:17:43,463 --> 00:17:45,696
the Bobby Neil case. Yeah.

359
00:17:48,167 --> 00:17:50,446
So, uh, Katie was gonna
take over your business, huh?

360
00:17:50,470 --> 00:17:54,806
And I was angry,
frustrated and helpless.

361
00:17:54,874 --> 00:17:58,075
Last year, you were real excited
about some guy you were dating.

362
00:17:58,144 --> 00:18:00,544
He was in, um, he was

363
00:18:00,613 --> 00:18:02,057
in advertising, I think?

364
00:18:02,081 --> 00:18:04,682
For about a month or so,
you were on top of the world

365
00:18:04,751 --> 00:18:07,062
and then all of a
sudden, it was over.

366
00:18:07,086 --> 00:18:09,053
Word does get
around, doesn't it?

367
00:18:09,122 --> 00:18:13,124
Bobby Neil says that Katie
took your boyfriend away.

368
00:18:13,192 --> 00:18:16,159
Well, Michelle.

369
00:18:16,228 --> 00:18:18,796
Well, Maggie.

370
00:18:18,865 --> 00:18:20,131
She took your boyfriend,

371
00:18:20,199 --> 00:18:22,119
she was gonna
take your business...

372
00:18:23,135 --> 00:18:26,637
Bobby remembers seeing you
get into your car and drive away

373
00:18:26,706 --> 00:18:27,986
after that meeting at her place.

374
00:18:28,040 --> 00:18:29,106
Why shouldn't I have?

375
00:18:29,175 --> 00:18:30,719
I came back here
and worked till closing.

376
00:18:30,743 --> 00:18:34,845
Well, this place is always
crowded late in the day.

377
00:18:34,914 --> 00:18:37,014
It would've been
easy to slip away

378
00:18:37,083 --> 00:18:39,128
for half an hour without
anybody noticing.

379
00:18:39,152 --> 00:18:40,312
You're off base, Michelle.

380
00:18:40,352 --> 00:18:43,921
You're way off base.

381
00:18:52,065 --> 00:18:53,431
All right, here we go now.

382
00:18:53,499 --> 00:18:54,576
Go ahead, go, go.

383
00:18:54,600 --> 00:18:55,966
That's good.

384
00:18:56,035 --> 00:18:57,601
A dozen more on this order

385
00:18:57,670 --> 00:18:59,603
and then we'll ship it out.

386
00:18:59,672 --> 00:19:01,739
Hey. Hey.

387
00:19:01,808 --> 00:19:04,241
Where does this stuff go?

388
00:19:04,310 --> 00:19:06,221
It gets put on a
truck and delivered

389
00:19:06,245 --> 00:19:07,690
to all Miss Katie's
cookie shops.

390
00:19:07,714 --> 00:19:09,425
They bake on the premises there.

391
00:19:09,449 --> 00:19:11,582
What about the
cookies you bake here?

392
00:19:11,650 --> 00:19:14,418
Well, we just box them
up and ship them out

393
00:19:14,487 --> 00:19:16,787
to the local restaurants
and department stores.

394
00:19:22,295 --> 00:19:26,464
What's to keep a guy
from just... taking the recipe

395
00:19:26,532 --> 00:19:28,944
and then going into
business for himself?

396
00:19:28,968 --> 00:19:30,634
Nobody knows the recipe.

397
00:19:30,703 --> 00:19:33,870
It's been locked up
in that safe over there.

398
00:19:33,939 --> 00:19:35,517
Then how do the
cookies get made?

399
00:19:35,541 --> 00:19:37,975
I put in a certain
amount of one thing

400
00:19:38,044 --> 00:19:39,543
and somebody else will put in

401
00:19:39,612 --> 00:19:40,923
a certain amount
of something else,

402
00:19:40,947 --> 00:19:42,257
somebody else
puts... Something else.

403
00:19:42,281 --> 00:19:44,125
So, everybody knows
part of the recipe,

404
00:19:44,149 --> 00:19:46,061
but nobody knows
the whole thing. Right.

405
00:19:46,085 --> 00:19:48,197
Y'all ever think about
getting your heads together

406
00:19:48,221 --> 00:19:49,920
and comparing notes?

407
00:19:49,989 --> 00:19:51,755
Katie White's
figured that out, too.

408
00:19:51,824 --> 00:19:54,002
See, if somebody tries
putting this recipe together,

409
00:19:54,026 --> 00:19:57,027
you get a $20,000
bonus for turning them in.

410
00:19:57,096 --> 00:20:00,131
That's a good one. Yeah.

411
00:20:00,199 --> 00:20:02,244
But you know one way
of whipping up a batch,

412
00:20:02,268 --> 00:20:04,346
you just get yourself
some of this batter,

413
00:20:04,370 --> 00:20:06,003
stick it in a plastic bag

414
00:20:06,072 --> 00:20:07,916
and sneak it out of here.

415
00:20:07,940 --> 00:20:09,818
Anybody who works
here can do that, huh?

416
00:20:09,842 --> 00:20:12,008
Not me.

417
00:20:27,493 --> 00:20:28,925
See ya later!

418
00:20:56,822 --> 00:20:59,757
♪ ♪

419
00:21:28,821 --> 00:21:31,755
♪ ♪

420
00:22:00,286 --> 00:22:03,153
♪ ♪

421
00:22:37,023 --> 00:22:40,490
Anyway, when I
came to, he was gone.

422
00:22:40,560 --> 00:22:45,295
Security guard
wasn't even there.

423
00:22:45,364 --> 00:22:47,075
Conrad, what's
the matter with you?

424
00:22:47,099 --> 00:22:48,477
I got kicked in the head!

425
00:22:48,501 --> 00:22:50,401
Now, wait a minute,

426
00:22:50,469 --> 00:22:52,709
weren't you the one that
asked me to go over there

427
00:22:52,738 --> 00:22:54,516
and work undercover
in the first place?

428
00:22:54,540 --> 00:22:56,451
Well, yeah, but if
you wanted something

429
00:22:56,475 --> 00:22:58,119
out of the personnel
office, why...

430
00:22:58,143 --> 00:22:59,954
Didn't you just
ask for it? Yeah.

431
00:22:59,978 --> 00:23:01,812
Because they'd get suspicious.

432
00:23:01,881 --> 00:23:03,747
They'd figure out I was a spy.

433
00:23:03,816 --> 00:23:05,515
Well, somebody must have anyway.

434
00:23:05,584 --> 00:23:06,928
Otherwise, you
wouldn't be putting

435
00:23:06,952 --> 00:23:09,152
that ice on your head.

436
00:23:09,221 --> 00:23:10,855
I guess you got that right.

437
00:23:10,923 --> 00:23:12,489
What were you looking for?

438
00:23:12,557 --> 00:23:13,891
Don't you think the only way

439
00:23:13,960 --> 00:23:15,893
the killer could
fool Katie White

440
00:23:15,962 --> 00:23:18,295
was by stealing
dough from her bakery

441
00:23:18,363 --> 00:23:20,831
and then mixing
ground-up hazelnuts into it?

442
00:23:20,900 --> 00:23:22,711
And then baking
that tin of cookies?

443
00:23:22,735 --> 00:23:25,368
Well, what were you looking
for in the personnel office?

444
00:23:25,437 --> 00:23:27,115
Well, I'm figuring
that the killer

445
00:23:27,139 --> 00:23:29,774
hired an accomplice
to steal the dough.

446
00:23:29,842 --> 00:23:32,376
What's that got to do
with the personnel office?

447
00:23:33,479 --> 00:23:35,546
For the past four weeks,

448
00:23:35,615 --> 00:23:37,948
nothing has been
working right in that kitchen.

449
00:23:38,017 --> 00:23:39,895
The ovens have been overheating,

450
00:23:39,919 --> 00:23:41,295
the mixers have
been going crazy,

451
00:23:41,319 --> 00:23:42,664
the refrigerators
are breaking down,

452
00:23:42,688 --> 00:23:45,422
and I figure it's because
the killer's accomplice

453
00:23:45,490 --> 00:23:47,390
was hired in the last month.

454
00:23:47,459 --> 00:23:49,538
He's been doing a
little industrial sabotage.

455
00:23:49,562 --> 00:23:51,795
Oh...

456
00:23:51,863 --> 00:23:53,630
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

457
00:23:53,699 --> 00:23:57,434
So, his name and when he
was hired would be in the files.

458
00:23:57,502 --> 00:23:59,537
Did you get them?

459
00:23:59,605 --> 00:24:02,506
Yeah.

460
00:24:02,575 --> 00:24:04,519
Only the guy who
clobbered me took them.

461
00:24:04,543 --> 00:24:06,509
You remember any names?

462
00:24:06,578 --> 00:24:08,946
When I came to, I could
barely remember my own.

463
00:24:09,014 --> 00:24:11,515
Oh.

464
00:24:11,583 --> 00:24:13,861
Look, in the
morning, I'll get up,

465
00:24:13,885 --> 00:24:16,445
and I'm gonna go to work again.

466
00:24:17,423 --> 00:24:20,223
What if the fellow who
clobbered you clobbers you again?

467
00:24:20,292 --> 00:24:23,794
Tomorrow, I've
got a better chance.

468
00:24:23,863 --> 00:24:27,597
It was dark, I
couldn't see his face.

469
00:24:27,666 --> 00:24:29,344
He doesn't think
I can identify him.

470
00:24:29,368 --> 00:24:30,734
You mean you can?

471
00:25:05,504 --> 00:25:06,737
You want something?

472
00:25:06,806 --> 00:25:07,738
Nice shoes.

473
00:25:07,807 --> 00:25:09,373
I like what they did

474
00:25:09,441 --> 00:25:12,001
to my face last night.

475
00:25:54,787 --> 00:25:56,586
Get up!

476
00:25:56,655 --> 00:25:58,555
Wake up. Hey, hey, hey.

477
00:25:58,623 --> 00:26:00,569
What the hell's going on here?

478
00:26:00,593 --> 00:26:02,504
Get out of here, both of you!

479
00:26:02,528 --> 00:26:03,861
You're fired!

480
00:26:10,136 --> 00:26:12,696
Will you look at this place?

481
00:26:15,541 --> 00:26:17,073
Who do you work for?

482
00:26:17,142 --> 00:26:18,074
I work for bakery.

483
00:26:18,143 --> 00:26:19,220
Uh-uh.

484
00:26:19,244 --> 00:26:20,522
Who's paying you to sabotage

485
00:26:20,546 --> 00:26:22,223
that equipment in there
and steal cookie dough?

486
00:26:22,247 --> 00:26:23,947
Uh, no steal.

487
00:26:24,016 --> 00:26:25,627
I work for bakery! Oh, no.

488
00:26:25,651 --> 00:26:27,262
Then why did you
jump me last night?

489
00:26:27,286 --> 00:26:29,285
You work for immigration.

490
00:26:29,354 --> 00:26:30,987
I don't work for immigration.

491
00:26:31,056 --> 00:26:33,123
I hear you.

492
00:26:33,192 --> 00:26:35,692
Always asking questions.

493
00:26:35,761 --> 00:26:38,295
I think maybe you
look for my friends.

494
00:26:38,363 --> 00:26:40,297
I followed you!

495
00:26:40,366 --> 00:26:42,299
I see you look for my address!

496
00:26:42,368 --> 00:26:44,401
Look, look... I stop you

497
00:26:44,469 --> 00:26:47,070
so that I can tell friends to
go so you cannot arrest them.

498
00:26:47,139 --> 00:26:48,750
Look, that says
private investigator,

499
00:26:48,774 --> 00:26:51,541
not immigration... I'm not after
your address or your friends.

500
00:26:51,610 --> 00:26:54,089
You know you almost put your
foot through my head last night?

501
00:26:54,113 --> 00:26:56,291
And a bucket through
my jaw in there?

502
00:26:56,315 --> 00:26:58,682
You may not be illegal,
but assault and battery is.

503
00:26:58,751 --> 00:27:01,284
You, my friend, had
better start talking.

504
00:27:03,655 --> 00:27:07,191
<i>Mr. Matlock, this is the
fastest moving idea in America.</i>

505
00:27:07,259 --> 00:27:08,825
<i>To your health.</i>

506
00:27:08,894 --> 00:27:12,195
Hey, cookies. Oat bran.

507
00:27:12,264 --> 00:27:14,175
It'll clean out your pipes,
lower your cholesterol,

508
00:27:14,199 --> 00:27:16,633
put a bounce in your step
and a song in your heart.

509
00:27:16,701 --> 00:27:18,735
Eat a dozen a day,
keeps the doctor away.

510
00:27:18,804 --> 00:27:21,504
No salt, no sugar, no
fat, no preservatives.

511
00:27:21,573 --> 00:27:24,133
Oh, it sounds too
good to be true.

512
00:27:24,176 --> 00:27:26,043
You gotta tune into
your body, Mr. Matlock.

513
00:27:26,111 --> 00:27:28,345
It wants healthy,
it craves thin,

514
00:27:28,414 --> 00:27:30,480
it demands the health cookie.

515
00:27:30,549 --> 00:27:32,749
Mmm.

516
00:27:34,219 --> 00:27:35,518
Tell me you love it.

517
00:27:35,587 --> 00:27:37,221
Mmm.

518
00:27:37,289 --> 00:27:38,555
What do you wanna talk about?

519
00:27:38,624 --> 00:27:39,624
Katie White?

520
00:27:39,658 --> 00:27:41,091
Wouldn't hurt.

521
00:27:41,160 --> 00:27:43,927
Well, Katie and I were old...

522
00:27:43,996 --> 00:27:47,297
Well, not so old...
But bitter enemies.

523
00:27:47,365 --> 00:27:49,632
I would spend
thousands of dollars

524
00:27:49,702 --> 00:27:52,169
researching the ideal
location for a cookie store.

525
00:27:52,237 --> 00:27:53,648
And the minute
before I sign the lease,

526
00:27:53,672 --> 00:27:54,938
guess who'd open a shop

527
00:27:55,007 --> 00:27:56,684
right across the street? Katie?

528
00:27:56,708 --> 00:27:59,476
I'd charge $3.00 a
pound for cookies,

529
00:27:59,545 --> 00:28:01,111
she'd charge $2.95.

530
00:28:01,179 --> 00:28:03,413
I'd stay open till 7:00,
she'd stay open till 8:00.

531
00:28:03,482 --> 00:28:04,715
I'd run a special

532
00:28:04,784 --> 00:28:06,516
and she'd run a better special.

533
00:28:06,584 --> 00:28:08,051
Aggressive, wasn't she?

534
00:28:09,355 --> 00:28:10,687
She hated me.

535
00:28:10,756 --> 00:28:13,690
Anything to knock
me out of the box.

536
00:28:13,759 --> 00:28:15,025
Have another cookie.

537
00:28:15,093 --> 00:28:16,493
Well...

538
00:28:16,562 --> 00:28:19,062
Clean your pipes.

539
00:28:19,131 --> 00:28:21,131
After you left her
conference room...

540
00:28:21,166 --> 00:28:23,200
I went for a drive

541
00:28:23,268 --> 00:28:26,403
and as I drove
away, I had a thought.

542
00:28:26,472 --> 00:28:29,406
What if, instead of waiting
for Katie to buy us out,

543
00:28:29,475 --> 00:28:31,742
the four of us got together
and bought her out?

544
00:28:31,811 --> 00:28:34,011
So, I got on my car phone
and called the others.

545
00:28:34,046 --> 00:28:35,745
They all have car phones?

546
00:28:35,814 --> 00:28:37,814
Well, Maggie Shore doesn't.

547
00:28:37,883 --> 00:28:40,161
Uh, she was back at her
muffin shop when I talked to her.

548
00:28:40,185 --> 00:28:41,451
But Bobby and Chrissie do.

549
00:28:41,520 --> 00:28:42,786
Mm-hmm.

550
00:28:42,855 --> 00:28:45,655
How long were you in your
car when you reached them?

551
00:28:45,724 --> 00:28:47,557
Ten, 15 minutes.

552
00:28:47,626 --> 00:28:49,526
Actually, I never did talk

553
00:28:49,595 --> 00:28:51,428
to Chrissie. You didn't?

554
00:28:51,496 --> 00:28:55,232
I got a recording saying
she was away from her car.

555
00:28:55,300 --> 00:28:56,566
But I got Bobby and Maggie.

556
00:28:58,603 --> 00:29:00,537
There's no flour in that either.

557
00:29:00,606 --> 00:29:01,606
No?

558
00:29:01,673 --> 00:29:03,707
Wanna know what
holds it together?

559
00:29:03,775 --> 00:29:04,941
Yeah.

560
00:29:05,010 --> 00:29:07,110
You think I'm gonna tell you?

561
00:29:11,717 --> 00:29:15,586
Oh, forgive me, I've just
come from Donald Ware's

562
00:29:15,654 --> 00:29:17,721
and I ate a carload
of his cookies.

563
00:29:17,789 --> 00:29:19,089
Like them?

564
00:29:19,158 --> 00:29:20,423
Not especially,

565
00:29:20,492 --> 00:29:23,494
but he said they'd be
so good for my pipes.

566
00:29:25,397 --> 00:29:27,130
Now, let's see.

567
00:29:27,198 --> 00:29:32,235
You said before, when you left
the meeting at Katie's, you came

568
00:29:32,304 --> 00:29:34,338
right back here. That's right.

569
00:29:34,406 --> 00:29:36,739
How long a drive is that?

570
00:29:36,808 --> 00:29:39,376
Hmm, about 30 minutes or so.

571
00:29:39,445 --> 00:29:44,214
So, if someone tried to get
you on your car phone, say,

572
00:29:44,283 --> 00:29:47,117
15 minutes after you left,

573
00:29:47,186 --> 00:29:49,686
they should be able to
reach you, shouldn't they?

574
00:29:49,754 --> 00:29:51,454
I suppose.

575
00:29:51,523 --> 00:29:56,693
Donald Ware said that,
that he tried to call you

576
00:29:56,762 --> 00:30:01,464
and he got a recording
saying you weren't in your car.

577
00:30:01,533 --> 00:30:04,534
Oh, wait a minute, I remember.

578
00:30:04,603 --> 00:30:06,169
I stopped for gas.

579
00:30:06,238 --> 00:30:07,771
When the engine's turned off,

580
00:30:07,839 --> 00:30:09,251
you automatically
get the recording.

581
00:30:09,275 --> 00:30:10,807
Did you use a credit card?

582
00:30:10,876 --> 00:30:12,156
Oh, no. Cash.

583
00:30:12,210 --> 00:30:14,444
Ah.

584
00:30:14,513 --> 00:30:15,779
Wow...

585
00:30:15,847 --> 00:30:18,114
Is this you?

586
00:30:19,451 --> 00:30:20,851
I was nine years old.

587
00:30:20,919 --> 00:30:22,385
That was my grandmother.

588
00:30:22,454 --> 00:30:24,766
Her chocolate chip cookies
had just won a blue ribbon

589
00:30:24,790 --> 00:30:26,556
at the state fair.

590
00:30:26,625 --> 00:30:28,257
Who's the other girl?

591
00:30:28,326 --> 00:30:29,860
Katie White.

592
00:30:29,928 --> 00:30:32,795
Oh.

593
00:30:32,864 --> 00:30:38,634
Your grandmother had won
a blue ribbon with her cookies.

594
00:30:38,703 --> 00:30:41,137
Katie went into the cookie
business and you didn't.

595
00:30:41,206 --> 00:30:42,339
How come?

596
00:30:42,408 --> 00:30:45,208
She beat me to it.

597
00:30:45,277 --> 00:30:48,211
And now, if you will
excuse me, Mr. Matlock,

598
00:30:48,280 --> 00:30:49,646
I have a lot of calls to make.

599
00:30:49,715 --> 00:30:52,115
Oh, sure, sure, sure.

600
00:30:52,183 --> 00:30:54,517
Sure, sure.

601
00:30:54,586 --> 00:30:56,153
Take it with you.

602
00:30:56,221 --> 00:30:58,388
Oh, no.

603
00:30:58,457 --> 00:31:00,590
I, uh, I...

604
00:31:00,659 --> 00:31:04,193
Well, maybe.

605
00:31:04,263 --> 00:31:06,263
Maybe for later

606
00:31:06,331 --> 00:31:09,199
or for a friend or...

607
00:31:09,267 --> 00:31:12,001
Well, the hell with
him, you gave it to me.

608
00:31:42,100 --> 00:31:44,868
♪ ♪

609
00:32:13,865 --> 00:32:16,799
♪ ♪

610
00:32:46,231 --> 00:32:49,165
♪ ♪

611
00:33:19,031 --> 00:33:20,964
♪ ♪

612
00:33:33,278 --> 00:33:36,179
♪ ♪

613
00:33:47,626 --> 00:33:50,393
Chrissie Dubin's in there
with John Schneider.

614
00:33:51,430 --> 00:33:52,862
Who's he?

615
00:33:52,931 --> 00:33:54,708
He's a baker at Katie
White's cookie factory.

616
00:33:54,732 --> 00:33:56,977
You know, that fella that
kicked me in the head?

617
00:33:57,001 --> 00:33:59,403
I know<i> somebody</i> did.

618
00:33:59,471 --> 00:34:02,873
Anyway, I thought he was the
one that was sabotaging the kitchen.

619
00:34:02,941 --> 00:34:04,485
He wasn't? No.

620
00:34:04,509 --> 00:34:06,521
And in exchange for
not pressing charges,

621
00:34:06,545 --> 00:34:08,356
he fingered John Schneider.

622
00:34:08,380 --> 00:34:09,312
Oh.

623
00:34:09,381 --> 00:34:10,592
You following Chrissie?

624
00:34:10,616 --> 00:34:11,715
Yeah.

625
00:34:11,784 --> 00:34:14,017
She wasn't where
she said she was

626
00:34:14,085 --> 00:34:15,584
when she left that meeting.

627
00:34:15,653 --> 00:34:17,520
You think this
Schneider fella's the one

628
00:34:17,589 --> 00:34:19,789
that stole the cookie
dough? I think so.

629
00:34:20,993 --> 00:34:23,927
She might be in
there paying him off.

630
00:34:23,996 --> 00:34:26,262
Want to say hi? Yeah.

631
00:34:34,873 --> 00:34:37,140
Yeah... Yeah, I'll do it.

632
00:34:42,781 --> 00:34:44,514
What do<i> you</i> want?

633
00:34:44,583 --> 00:34:48,151
We'd like to speak with you
and Ms. Dubin, if we might.

634
00:34:48,220 --> 00:34:50,920
What is it, Mr. Matlock?

635
00:34:50,989 --> 00:34:53,823
And make it fast, because
I'm calling my attorney.

636
00:34:53,892 --> 00:34:56,037
Or don't you know there
are laws against harassment?

637
00:34:56,061 --> 00:34:57,505
Do that; you're gonna need him.

638
00:34:57,529 --> 00:34:58,762
What are you talking about?

639
00:34:58,831 --> 00:35:01,030
You hired Mr. Schneider here

640
00:35:01,099 --> 00:35:04,500
to steal the dough
that killed Miss White.

641
00:35:04,569 --> 00:35:07,536
What are you talking about?

642
00:35:07,605 --> 00:35:10,706
You were not in your car
when Donald Ware called.

643
00:35:10,775 --> 00:35:12,620
You weren't at the
gas station, either.

644
00:35:12,644 --> 00:35:14,522
You were in Katie
White's office,

645
00:35:14,546 --> 00:35:15,745
planting those cookies.

646
00:35:15,814 --> 00:35:18,026
Is that what you're
going to say in court?

647
00:35:18,050 --> 00:35:19,182
You bet.

648
00:35:19,250 --> 00:35:21,495
Then you're going to
make a fool of yourself.

649
00:35:21,519 --> 00:35:23,253
You really will, Mr. Matlock.

650
00:35:23,321 --> 00:35:25,361
See, because I
wasn't in Katie's office,

651
00:35:25,423 --> 00:35:27,068
and I wasn't at the gas station.

652
00:35:27,092 --> 00:35:28,269
I came straight here.

653
00:35:28,293 --> 00:35:30,237
We're lovers, Mr. Matlock.

654
00:35:30,261 --> 00:35:32,440
We have to meet here right now.

655
00:35:32,464 --> 00:35:34,909
John's married, but soon
all that's going to change.

656
00:35:34,933 --> 00:35:36,244
Good enough for
you, Mr. Matlock?

657
00:35:36,268 --> 00:35:37,778
And if our word
isn't good enough,

658
00:35:37,802 --> 00:35:39,647
why don't you talk
to the desk clerk.

659
00:35:39,671 --> 00:35:41,249
Or the guy that
brought us dinner.

660
00:35:41,273 --> 00:35:43,139
Or the maid who
brought us fresh towels.

661
00:35:43,208 --> 00:35:44,208
Ask anybody.

662
00:35:44,276 --> 00:35:45,319
Now...

663
00:35:45,343 --> 00:35:47,310
if you'll excuse us.

664
00:36:04,196 --> 00:36:05,428
Thank you.

665
00:36:05,496 --> 00:36:08,231
If you need me, I'll
be right across the hall.

666
00:36:10,568 --> 00:36:12,102
I can't believe it.

667
00:36:12,170 --> 00:36:14,804
I can't believe I'd do
something that dumb.

668
00:36:14,873 --> 00:36:16,506
Now... It was<i> dumb.</i>

669
00:36:16,575 --> 00:36:18,774
Now... Well, how
c... how could I,

670
00:36:18,843 --> 00:36:21,177
without real proof, accuse
this woman of murder

671
00:36:21,246 --> 00:36:23,206
and the man of
being her accomplice?

672
00:36:23,248 --> 00:36:25,881
When all they were doing
was meeting at a motel

673
00:36:25,950 --> 00:36:28,684
'cause he's married and
because they wanted to...

674
00:36:28,753 --> 00:36:29,786
you know.

675
00:36:29,855 --> 00:36:31,521
It's just one of those...

676
00:36:31,590 --> 00:36:32,766
Dumb.

677
00:36:32,790 --> 00:36:35,157
I knew better than
that 20 years ago.

678
00:36:35,226 --> 00:36:37,493
Maybe I'm getting too
old for this business.

679
00:36:37,562 --> 00:36:38,895
Now, stop that.

680
00:36:38,964 --> 00:36:40,162
You're not too old.

681
00:36:40,231 --> 00:36:41,965
Your mind is still sharp.

682
00:36:42,033 --> 00:36:43,333
I mean, the cases

683
00:36:43,401 --> 00:36:44,734
you win.

684
00:36:44,803 --> 00:36:46,269
Mm, well...

685
00:36:46,337 --> 00:36:47,536
And look at you.

686
00:36:47,605 --> 00:36:50,573
You're healthy,
you're tall... your hair

687
00:36:50,642 --> 00:36:52,575
and your figure.

688
00:36:53,812 --> 00:36:56,412
Well, yeah, but...

689
00:36:56,481 --> 00:36:57,914
it's still dumb.

690
00:36:57,983 --> 00:37:00,349
You can't hold that
against yourself.

691
00:37:00,418 --> 00:37:02,184
Every now and then, everybody

692
00:37:02,253 --> 00:37:04,386
does something really dumb.

693
00:37:04,455 --> 00:37:05,921
No, I'm sorry, I didn't...

694
00:37:05,991 --> 00:37:07,868
No, it was dumb. It's okay.

695
00:37:07,892 --> 00:37:09,425
It's dumb.

696
00:37:11,729 --> 00:37:13,007
What's all that?

697
00:37:13,031 --> 00:37:14,163
Ms. White's correspondence.

698
00:37:14,232 --> 00:37:15,931
The attorney who's
handling her estate said

699
00:37:16,001 --> 00:37:18,167
I should just leave
it in here for now.

700
00:37:18,236 --> 00:37:19,902
What are these?

701
00:37:19,971 --> 00:37:21,616
Prints of the photo
she was gonna send out

702
00:37:21,640 --> 00:37:23,284
with the press release
on the takeover.

703
00:37:23,308 --> 00:37:25,641
It was taken just the
day before she died.

704
00:37:25,710 --> 00:37:27,077
Beautiful woman.

705
00:37:31,717 --> 00:37:33,682
I wasn't dumb.

706
00:37:33,751 --> 00:37:36,820
Just premature.

707
00:37:40,926 --> 00:37:42,224
Uh...

708
00:37:42,293 --> 00:37:45,194
Ms. Dubin, I understand
that you used to be in business

709
00:37:45,263 --> 00:37:46,930
with, uh, Katie White.

710
00:37:46,998 --> 00:37:48,531
For about a year after college,

711
00:37:48,600 --> 00:37:50,132
we ran a catering business, yes.

712
00:37:50,201 --> 00:37:52,112
What became of the business?

713
00:37:52,136 --> 00:37:54,103
I sold my share to Katie,

714
00:37:54,172 --> 00:37:56,217
and after about six
months, she gave it up.

715
00:37:56,241 --> 00:37:58,207
Couldn't make it without you?

716
00:37:58,276 --> 00:38:01,144
Katie was a great
promoter but a lousy cook.

717
00:38:01,212 --> 00:38:04,881
If she was such a lousy
cook, where'd she get

718
00:38:04,950 --> 00:38:07,550
the cookie recipe that
made her a millionaire

719
00:38:07,619 --> 00:38:09,418
several times over?

720
00:38:09,487 --> 00:38:10,820
She got lucky.

721
00:38:10,889 --> 00:38:12,154
Huh.

722
00:38:12,223 --> 00:38:15,925
Your grandmother won first prize

723
00:38:15,993 --> 00:38:20,863
for her chocolate chip cookies
in the 1967 Georgia State Fair,

724
00:38:20,932 --> 00:38:22,109
is that not true?

725
00:38:22,133 --> 00:38:24,212
Yes. I contacted
the fair people,

726
00:38:24,236 --> 00:38:27,637
and the Homemaking
Division keeps a record

727
00:38:27,705 --> 00:38:30,940
of all their blue ribbon
winners and their recipes,

728
00:38:31,009 --> 00:38:33,509
and those recipes
are very seriously

729
00:38:33,578 --> 00:38:35,478
kept under lock and key,

730
00:38:35,547 --> 00:38:37,179
very confidential.

731
00:38:37,248 --> 00:38:40,116
Like many
government, uh, secrets.

732
00:38:40,185 --> 00:38:41,951
I had to subpoena

733
00:38:42,020 --> 00:38:46,256
to get a copy of your,
of your grandmother's.

734
00:38:46,324 --> 00:38:47,723
Your Honor.

735
00:38:49,160 --> 00:38:50,660
Uh...

736
00:38:50,729 --> 00:38:52,528
does it look familiar?

737
00:38:52,597 --> 00:38:54,709
That was over 20 years ago.

738
00:38:54,733 --> 00:38:56,298
Yeah.

739
00:38:56,368 --> 00:39:00,470
Well, this is a copy
of the cookie recipe

740
00:39:00,538 --> 00:39:03,639
for Katie White's
chocolate chip cookies.

741
00:39:05,643 --> 00:39:08,244
They're exactly the
same, aren't they?

742
00:39:08,312 --> 00:39:09,512
Yes.

743
00:39:09,580 --> 00:39:11,080
They're identical.

744
00:39:11,149 --> 00:39:13,182
Katie White stole that recipe.

745
00:39:13,251 --> 00:39:16,051
She took your grandma's
recipe, that was rightly yours,

746
00:39:16,121 --> 00:39:19,088
and used it to establish
one of the most successful

747
00:39:19,157 --> 00:39:21,001
business ventures
the state of Georgia

748
00:39:21,025 --> 00:39:22,625
has ever seen, didn't she?

749
00:39:22,693 --> 00:39:25,028
Objection. Irrelevant.

750
00:39:25,097 --> 00:39:27,175
Irrelevant?! Goes to motive.

751
00:39:27,199 --> 00:39:28,876
What's the matter
with you? Please!

752
00:39:28,900 --> 00:39:31,012
Direct your remarks to
the bench, Mr. Matlock.

753
00:39:31,036 --> 00:39:32,602
It goes to motive, Your Honor.

754
00:39:32,670 --> 00:39:34,448
What's the matter
with you? Mr. Matlock.

755
00:39:34,472 --> 00:39:35,950
Yes, sir? The bench.

756
00:39:35,974 --> 00:39:38,941
But it does go to
motive, Your Honor.

757
00:39:40,045 --> 00:39:41,944
Objection overruled.

758
00:39:42,013 --> 00:39:44,547
She took it right out from
under you, didn't she?

759
00:39:44,615 --> 00:39:47,094
Yes. Why didn't you
do anything about it?

760
00:39:47,118 --> 00:39:49,084
My lawyer said that the case

761
00:39:49,154 --> 00:39:51,114
would be almost
impossible to prove.

762
00:39:51,155 --> 00:39:54,057
And-And-And when...
when the rumors started

763
00:39:54,125 --> 00:39:57,393
that she intended to take
over your pie company,

764
00:39:57,461 --> 00:39:59,095
what'd you do about that?

765
00:39:59,164 --> 00:40:01,464
Once again, there
was nothing I<i> could</i> do.

766
00:40:01,533 --> 00:40:04,733
I think, this time, you
tried fighting back.

767
00:40:04,802 --> 00:40:07,370
Who's John Schneider?

768
00:40:08,473 --> 00:40:10,072
He's my friend.

769
00:40:10,141 --> 00:40:11,307
Friend?

770
00:40:11,376 --> 00:40:12,575
<i>Motel</i> friend.

771
00:40:12,644 --> 00:40:13,644
Irrelevant!

772
00:40:14,612 --> 00:40:15,310
Oh, come on!

773
00:40:15,379 --> 00:40:17,146
The bench.

774
00:40:17,215 --> 00:40:18,759
A few more moments, Your Honor.

775
00:40:18,783 --> 00:40:19,849
You better watch it.

776
00:40:19,917 --> 00:40:20,850
Yes, sir.

777
00:40:20,919 --> 00:40:21,984
Go ahead.

778
00:40:22,053 --> 00:40:23,386
Yeah.

779
00:40:23,455 --> 00:40:25,054
Where does he work?

780
00:40:25,123 --> 00:40:28,958
At Miss Katie's Cookies
central bakery and warehouse.

781
00:40:29,026 --> 00:40:31,160
Mm-hmm. Where'd
he work before that?

782
00:40:31,229 --> 00:40:32,662
For me.

783
00:40:32,731 --> 00:40:35,265
When the takeover
rumors started,

784
00:40:35,333 --> 00:40:37,900
you asked your<i>
boyfriend,</i> John Schneider,

785
00:40:37,969 --> 00:40:40,936
to get a job at
Katie White's bakery,

786
00:40:41,005 --> 00:40:43,205
so he could sabotage
the operation,

787
00:40:43,274 --> 00:40:44,718
didn't you? No.

788
00:40:44,742 --> 00:40:46,542
John's a baker.

789
00:40:46,611 --> 00:40:49,545
We have a complicated
relationship, as you well know,

790
00:40:49,614 --> 00:40:52,848
and so, for that reason,
he took a job at Katie's.

791
00:40:52,917 --> 00:40:55,718
Then why did all the equipment
suddenly start breaking apart

792
00:40:55,787 --> 00:40:57,687
within a week
after he was hired?

793
00:40:57,756 --> 00:40:59,500
I don't know
anything about that.

794
00:40:59,524 --> 00:41:01,301
You knew that Katie
White was deathly allergic

795
00:41:01,325 --> 00:41:02,403
to hazelnuts, didn't you?

796
00:41:02,427 --> 00:41:03,871
Everybody knew. Would she

797
00:41:03,895 --> 00:41:06,095
ever have eaten that
cookie that killed her,

798
00:41:06,164 --> 00:41:08,697
if it hadn't looked exactly
like all the other cookies

799
00:41:08,766 --> 00:41:10,065
that came from her bakery?

800
00:41:10,134 --> 00:41:11,445
I... I don't know.

801
00:41:11,469 --> 00:41:13,589
And-And-And the only
way it could look like

802
00:41:13,638 --> 00:41:16,572
all the other cookies, was
for it to have been made

803
00:41:16,641 --> 00:41:18,719
from batter that came
from her bakery, right?

804
00:41:18,743 --> 00:41:20,743
I don't know.

805
00:41:20,812 --> 00:41:22,857
John Schneider stole
batter from her bakery

806
00:41:22,881 --> 00:41:26,482
and gave it to you, so that
you could, once and for all,

807
00:41:26,551 --> 00:41:28,718
avenge yourself on
Katie White, didn't he?

808
00:41:28,786 --> 00:41:30,965
Objection! No foundation.

809
00:41:30,989 --> 00:41:32,221
Pure speculation.

810
00:41:32,290 --> 00:41:34,156
Not so! It's not speculation!

811
00:41:34,225 --> 00:41:35,336
Mr. Matlock!

812
00:41:35,360 --> 00:41:36,693
It's not speculation.

813
00:41:36,761 --> 00:41:37,971
Are you sure?

814
00:41:37,995 --> 00:41:39,395
Yes, I'm sure!

815
00:41:39,463 --> 00:41:42,131
We do not yell at the bench.

816
00:41:42,200 --> 00:41:44,800
Oh, I'm sorry. I
apologize, Your Honor.

817
00:41:44,869 --> 00:41:46,936
I apologize. You're
very close to contempt.

818
00:41:47,005 --> 00:41:48,103
Oh, no... oh, no.

819
00:41:48,172 --> 00:41:49,705
This will all tie together.

820
00:41:50,975 --> 00:41:52,908
All right. Overruled.

821
00:41:54,512 --> 00:41:57,513
Uh, for a long time,

822
00:41:57,582 --> 00:42:00,249
I thought those hazelnut cookies

823
00:42:00,317 --> 00:42:03,586
were planted <i>after</i>
the takeover meeting.

824
00:42:03,655 --> 00:42:07,389
But you knew that
cookie tin was in her office

825
00:42:07,458 --> 00:42:09,291
<i>before</i> the meeting,

826
00:42:09,360 --> 00:42:12,361
because John Schneider,
who worked there, told you,

827
00:42:12,430 --> 00:42:13,540
didn't he? No.

828
00:42:13,564 --> 00:42:15,998
You made a big batch of cookies

829
00:42:16,067 --> 00:42:18,000
with batter from her bakery,

830
00:42:18,069 --> 00:42:20,029
laced them with
ground-up hazelnuts,

831
00:42:20,071 --> 00:42:23,372
went into her office
before the meeting,

832
00:42:23,441 --> 00:42:26,942
replaced the cookies
in the tin with yours,

833
00:42:27,011 --> 00:42:29,112
got rid of the originals,

834
00:42:29,180 --> 00:42:33,048
took what was left over of
yours over to Bobby Neal's

835
00:42:33,118 --> 00:42:35,918
and planted them in
his garbage, didn't you?

836
00:42:35,987 --> 00:42:37,920
No, I did no such thing.

837
00:42:37,989 --> 00:42:40,956
Except for the meeting, I
never set foot in Katie's office.

838
00:42:42,994 --> 00:42:45,127
This is a picture...

839
00:42:45,196 --> 00:42:46,829
of Katie White...

840
00:42:46,898 --> 00:42:49,009
taken the day before she died.

841
00:42:49,033 --> 00:42:51,000
What's that on her desk?

842
00:42:51,069 --> 00:42:53,269
A paperweight.

843
00:42:53,338 --> 00:42:55,605
What's in the paperweight?

844
00:42:58,442 --> 00:43:01,243
A half a dollar bill.

845
00:43:01,312 --> 00:43:04,480
That is half...

846
00:43:04,549 --> 00:43:06,849
the first bill...

847
00:43:06,917 --> 00:43:09,485
that you and Katie made

848
00:43:09,554 --> 00:43:11,987
in your catering
business, isn't it?

849
00:43:12,056 --> 00:43:13,923
Yes.

850
00:43:13,991 --> 00:43:17,192
After you left this morning,

851
00:43:17,261 --> 00:43:20,462
the police went to your
house and retrieved this

852
00:43:20,532 --> 00:43:21,898
from your office.

853
00:43:21,966 --> 00:43:23,632
Tell the court what it is.

854
00:43:26,837 --> 00:43:30,840
It's the first dollar bill I
made as the Pie Lady.

855
00:43:30,908 --> 00:43:32,675
Is it?

856
00:43:35,046 --> 00:43:36,779
Read...

857
00:43:36,848 --> 00:43:38,581
the serial number

858
00:43:38,650 --> 00:43:40,650
on this half a bill

859
00:43:40,718 --> 00:43:43,278
that's in the
paperweight... use this.

860
00:43:47,859 --> 00:43:50,259
B-9-6...

861
00:43:50,327 --> 00:43:52,127
2-1...

862
00:43:52,196 --> 00:43:55,564
3-4-2-2-D.

863
00:43:56,601 --> 00:43:59,161
Now read this serial number.

864
00:44:04,709 --> 00:44:07,176
B-9-6-2-1-3-4-

865
00:44:07,245 --> 00:44:08,777
2-2-D.

866
00:44:10,882 --> 00:44:14,182
They're the same.

867
00:44:14,251 --> 00:44:16,786
If you examine
this dollar closely,

868
00:44:16,854 --> 00:44:19,555
you'll see it's two halves

869
00:44:19,624 --> 00:44:21,356
that have been taped together...

870
00:44:21,426 --> 00:44:24,092
Your half and
Katie White's half.

871
00:44:26,764 --> 00:44:30,533
You took this bill
from her office...

872
00:44:30,602 --> 00:44:34,270
when you planted the
cookie that would kill her.

873
00:44:34,339 --> 00:44:36,405
I thought I was dumb

874
00:44:36,474 --> 00:44:38,518
when I accused you at the motel.

875
00:44:38,542 --> 00:44:40,287
Forgive me for saying it,

876
00:44:40,311 --> 00:44:41,477
but you were dumber

877
00:44:41,546 --> 00:44:43,713
when you took this
bill from her office.

878
00:44:43,781 --> 00:44:45,781
It was a symbol of your rivalry.

879
00:44:48,319 --> 00:44:50,586
And...

880
00:44:50,654 --> 00:44:54,623
with it, you finally beat
Katie White, didn't you?

881
00:44:54,692 --> 00:44:57,593
It's one of those
awful twists of fate.

882
00:44:57,661 --> 00:44:59,695
You finally won.

883
00:45:01,766 --> 00:45:04,900
But in winning, you lost.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
